    	Alternate solution:  fire a wand of digging straight down.
The luck penalty is balanced out by 1 boulder filling the hole
instead of being broken.

    	Failing that:  strip down.  Drop breakable stuff and stuff
you won't need before returning.  If you have a blindfold + ESP,
check what's down the corridor.  If the corridor is clear, throw
your equipment down.  Start with things which intelligent monsters 
can't use against you.  Delay throwing ranged-attack items, even 
if the damage is very low (e.g.:  orcish daggers at unskilled).

    	Have a second look with the blindfold before throwing it.  
If the corridor has an intelligent monster, or something that
you can't beat nude, try ranged attacks when the monster is within
range (str/2 squares for light thrown weapons).

    	When you go down the corridor, the last boulder will be
pushed down the corridor.  Monsters blocking the boulder's move-
ment will mostly shuffle back a step, given time.  This lets
you get to your equipment, re-equip, and push the boulder to the
corner of that corridor.  Give any monsters on the next length 
of corridor a dozen turns or so to move up so you can kill them.

    	You specified no boulder-breaker.  I'm almost certain that
you can't move on the diagonal past the corner boulder.  Thus, you
repeat the above, throwing your stuff on the diagonal.

    	This fails for some cases (a flock of orcs, or a non-moving
jelly which you don't have the right resistance for), but usually
works. 

    	As an aside, I normally delay entering the Sokoban zoo until
I have a source of stealth.  

